# Accessibility

- Include skip link, landmarks, and logical heading hierarchy on every page shell.
- Use meaningful `alt` text; treat empty string or `decorative` as decorative images.
- Prefer semantic HTML (`main`, `nav`, `header`, `footer`, `figure`, `figcaption`).
- Maintain visible `:focus-visible` styles and honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Dialog/lightbox components must use `role="dialog"` and `aria-modal="true"` when implemented.
- Do not remove accessibility scaffolding when applying final visual design from Figma.
